# Owner scope and authoring direction

The owner requested the **Advanced QFT and supersymmetry** category and then
directed: **“Start building as soon as it's ready.”** This authorizes the native
physics build in this isolated checkout. The dated scaffold remains a research
design; its earlier scaffold-only dispatch language does not revoke this later
build authorization. Every ordinary native prerequisite, source, review, repair,
gate and owner hold remains binding. Do not publish or push. New content remains
draft.

The approved starting scope is the 55 A/B pairs in this run's native manifests
and scope ledger: 36 physics pairs in `advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry` and 19
purely mathematical support pairs in `quantum-field-theory-mathematics`.
Read `research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md`, the complete
`research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md`, the
exact assigned contracts in `scaffold/proposed-inventory.json`, and all relevant
specialist notes beneath that same dated directory. Its 143 future item
contracts are authoring obligations, not accepted proofs. The three separately
listed unreviewed question candidates are not production items or suppliers.
Only the precisely formulated, source-checked Clay question has an adopted
open-problem classification.

Preserve substantial coverage of Non-Abelian gauge theory, EFT, supersymmetry,
localization, BPS states, generalized symmetries, defects and anomalies through
the source-qualified research frontier. Do not narrow approved claims to avoid
necessary prerequisite work. Build substantial examples on the assigned B
companions; their initial empty canonical item arrays are planning placeholders,
not permission to leave finished pages empty. B-only items cannot supply other
pages. Missing established local proofs are authoring obligations, never newly
invented open problems.

Every technical term needs an explicit mathematical definition with objects,
spaces, maps, regularity, domains, hypotheses and conventions before use. Every
result needs its complete local argument and exact actual supplier uses.
Keep mathematical material purely mathematical; physical deductions use the
physics-theorem or thought-experiment class and explicitly adopted premises.
Preserve the metric, spinor, central-charge, BRST, trace, orientation and
monopole-energy conventions checked in the prose. Continuum path integrals,
localization limits, dualities and physical BPS dictionaries do not follow from
finite models, formal series, ordinary index theory or Hall identities alone.

The external dependency table records current pins and acceptance limits.
Published labels, matching import hashes and judge-only/precheck stamps do not
grant proof acceptance. Resolve each conditional supplier use honestly before
claiming readiness: inspect the actual proof, identify the smallest missing
mathematical result, provide a complete new local mathematical alternative when
appropriate, or escalate to root with precise consumers and the missing
interface. Never edit imported snapshots or original root mathematics. The
existing import receipt identifies the actual original source repository;
source reading is read-only and is not an import or acceptance receipt.

Experiments need source-backed apparatus, preparation, operational observables,
controls, calibration, selection, sampling/likelihood assumptions, inference,
uncertainty, systematics and qualified findings. Retrieve the full preliminary
CMS report before turning its source-limited candidate into a complete empirical
carrier. Do not invent data, numerical limits, full-text reading or independent
reanalysis. A null search excludes its stated model family, not supersymmetry
as a framework. The recent INSPIRE ledger records metadata/abstract discovery
only; read full sources and check status before using their claims.

`tools/physics-autopilot/` alone owns dispatch and transitions. The workspace
configuration caps concurrent workers at twenty; native model profiles remain
unchanged, including GPT-6-Luna/max for initial drift and construction.
All writing and state for this run stay in this isolated checkout. The original
workspace and its plans, imported snapshots and live runs remain untouched.

## Continuous owner supervision

The owner subsequently directed **“supervise continuously.”** Root therefore
monitors this run, resolves escalations, performs truthful owner metadata
recertification, and releases ordinary native gates when their conditions are
met. This does not waive a review, proof obligation, gate, or source limitation.
The four original Step-1 drift holds and their immutable input preimages are
recorded in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/`.
Their resolution evidence supplements the unchanged native report; it does
not rewrite historical findings or create worker coverage.

## Additional prerequisite theories and placement correction

The owner explicitly authorized **“Build new pairs for missing theories if
necessary, either within this category or in published categories.”** Root may
therefore add genuinely necessary mathematical/physical prerequisite A/B pairs
through the native scope controls, in this category or the relevant existing
category. Preserve approved claims; do not hide a missing theory or duplicate
sound existing theory merely to replace a missing stamp. New content stays
draft, imports stay immutable, and scope changes retain their required native
evidence and review.

The registered EFT theorem
`pthm-aqft-wilsonian-superpotential-nonrenormalization` now belongs on
`aqft-susy-effective-theories`, immediately after its exact
`def-aqft-susy-wilsonian-action` prerequisite. This corrects an earlier-page
placement that would create a page cycle. Keep its ID, statement and dependencies
unchanged. The earlier Ward page retains its separate N=1 Wilsonian theorem.
Read `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/placement-review.md`.

## Engine concurrency update

The owner explicitly increased physics and mathematics engine worker limits to
20 and requested an engine reload. Both concurrency and globalConcurrency are
20 in this workspace; existing dispatches are preserved and adopted on reload.
Native profiles, proof obligations, review gates and draft status are unchanged.

