+---
+id: thm-qftx-strong-coupling-wilson-area-law
+kind: theorem
+title: Exact finite-lattice SU(2) Wilson area law in two dimensions
+status: draft
+origin: session
+dependency_level: 4
+domain: mathematics
+library: mathematics
+category: quantum-field-theory-mathematics
+axiom_base: "ZF + AC_omega inherited through the stated finite lattice data; the finite integration proof uses no stronger choice principle."
+deps:
+  - def-countable-choice
+  - def-qftx-nonabelian-lattice-gauge-data
+  - def-qftx-wilson-loop
+  - def-qftx-su2-wilson-plaquette-measure
+  - lem-qftx-lattice-data-well-defined
+  - lem-qftx-wilson-loop-gauge-invariance
+  - lem-qftx-planar-plaquette-factorization
+  - lem-qftx-su2-one-plaquette-average
+dependency_roles:
+  def-countable-choice: mathematical-premise
+  def-qftx-nonabelian-lattice-gauge-data: mathematical-premise
+  def-qftx-wilson-loop: mathematical-premise
+  def-qftx-su2-wilson-plaquette-measure: mathematical-premise
+  lem-qftx-lattice-data-well-defined: mathematical-premise
+  lem-qftx-wilson-loop-gauge-invariance: mathematical-premise
+  lem-qftx-planar-plaquette-factorization: mathematical-premise
+  lem-qftx-su2-one-plaquette-average: mathematical-premise
+provenance:
+  statement: ai-altered
+  proof: ai-generated
+sources:
+  references:
+    - title: "H. B. Meyer, Lattice QCD: A Brief Introduction, in Lattice QCD for Nuclear Physics, Lecture Notes in Physics 889"
+      url: "https://ndl.ethernet.edu.et/bitstream/123456789/73862/1/82.pdf.pdf"
+      locator: "§§1.2.3–1.2.4, printed pp. 11–14, for link and plaquette conventions; §1.4.1.1, pp. 22–24, for the strong-coupling minimal-surface calculation and its fixed-regulator boundary."
+    - title: "Robert Lohmayer, Eigenvalue Distributions of Wilson Loops"
+      url: "https://epub.uni-regensburg.de/16031/1/EigenvalueDistributionsOfWilsonLoops.pdf"
+      locator: "§§4.1–4.2.2, printed pp. 59–64, for exact two-dimensional plaquette factorization, rectangular Wilson-loop area dependence, and unitary-group integrals."
+verification:
+  precheck: pending
+proof_strategy: direct
+---
+
+## Statement
+
+Assume $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$. Let $M,N\geq1$ be integers and use the finite $M$-by-$N$ square lattice with free boundary, one $SU(2)$ link matrix per positively oriented edge, product normalized round measure, no matter fields, and the Wilson action $S_\beta(U)=\beta\sum_p(1-\tfrac12\operatorname{Tr}_2 U_p)$. Use the defining two-dimensional representation and normalized Wilson loop $W(C)=\tfrac12\operatorname{Tr}_2 U_C$, with edge matrices multiplied in traversal order. Let $\beta=4/g_0^2$ for dimensionless $g_0>0$, and restrict to the explicit strong-coupling window $0<\beta\leq1$ (equivalently $g_0^2\geq4$). For any axis-aligned rectangle $C_{a,b;c,d}$ contained in the lattice, where $0\leq a<b\leq M$ and $0\leq c<d\leq N$, its area in plaquette units is $A=(b-a)(d-c)$. The defining representation has nontrivial $\mathbb Z_2$ center charge because $-I_2$ acts as $-I_2$. Put
+
+$$
+\lambda(\beta):=\frac{\int_{SU(2)}\tfrac12\operatorname{Tr}_2(U)e^{\beta\operatorname{Tr}_2(U)/2}\,d\mu_2(U)}{\int_{SU(2)}e^{\beta\operatorname{Tr}_2(U)/2}\,d\mu_2(U)},
+$$
+
+where $\mu_2$ is normalized round measure on $SU(2)\cong S^3$. Then $0<\lambda(\beta)<1$ and the exact finite-lattice expectation is
+
+$$
+\langle W(C_{a,b;c,d})\rangle_\beta=\lambda(\beta)^A=\exp\!\bigl(-\sigma_{\rm lat}(\beta)A\bigr),\qquad \sigma_{\rm lat}(\beta):=-\log\lambda(\beta)>0.
+$$
+
+The parameter $\beta$ and the lattice string tension $\sigma_{\rm lat}$ are dimensionless. The identity holds for every finite container and every stated rectangle; no infinite-area, infinite-volume, or continuum limit is taken, and no continuum confinement or mass-gap claim follows.
+
+## Statement references
+
+[[def-qftx-nonabelian-lattice-gauge-data|Finite link configurations, gauge action, and product measure]]
+
+[[def-qftx-wilson-loop|Normalized trace of ordered lattice holonomy]]
+
+[[def-qftx-su2-wilson-plaquette-measure|SU(2) Wilson action and one-plaquette probability]]
+
+[[lem-qftx-planar-plaquette-factorization|Independent plaquette variables on a finite rectangle]]
+
+[[lem-qftx-su2-one-plaquette-average|One-plaquette matrix average and strong-coupling coefficient]]
+
+[Meyer, §1.4.1.1, printed pp. 22–24; the cited 4D leading-order argument is contextual, and the finite 2D identity is proved here](https://ndl.ethernet.edu.et/bitstream/123456789/73862/1/82.pdf.pdf)
+
+[Lohmayer, §§4.1–4.2.2, printed pp. 59–64; the exact 2D factorization mechanism is rederived for the stated finite free-boundary lattice](https://epub.uni-regensburg.de/16031/1/EigenvalueDistributionsOfWilsonLoops.pdf)
+
+## Facts & Assumptions
+
+**Given:** $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$, the finite free-boundary square lattice, the defining $SU(2)$ representation, the Wilson action with $0<\beta\leq1$, and a rectangular loop $C_{a,b;c,d}$.
+
+[A1] $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$ is inherited through the finite non-Abelian lattice datum; the present integration proof uses only finite products and explicit coordinate changes. [[def-countable-choice]]
+
+[F1] [[def-qftx-nonabelian-lattice-gauge-data]]: link configurations are $G$-valued, the vertex group acts by endpoint multiplication, and normalized product Haar measure is used on the finite link set.
+
+[F2] [[def-qftx-wilson-loop]]: $W(C)=\tfrac12\operatorname{Tr}_2(U_C)$ for the defining representation, with edge matrices multiplied in traversal order.
+
+[F3] [[def-qftx-su2-wilson-plaquette-measure]]: $S_\beta=\beta\sum_p(1-\tau(U_p))$, $\tau(U)=\tfrac12\operatorname{Tr}_2U$, and the one-plaquette law is $d\nu_\beta=z_\beta^{-1}e^{\beta\tau}d\mu_2$.
+
+[F4] [[lem-qftx-lattice-data-well-defined]]: the link action and product measure define a normalized finite-lattice probability.
+
+[F5] [[lem-qftx-wilson-loop-gauge-invariance]]: the closed-loop trace is gauge invariant.
+
+[F6] [[lem-qftx-planar-plaquette-factorization]]: in a chosen tree gauge, the rectangle's plaquette holonomies are independent with law $\nu_\beta$ when all face weights are the same Wilson weight.
+
+[F7] [[lem-qftx-su2-one-plaquette-average]]: $\mathbb E_{\nu_\beta}[U]=\lambda(\beta)I_2$ and $0<\lambda(\beta)<1$.
+
+## Proof
+
+1.1 The Wilson action weight is $e^{-\beta N_p}\prod_p e^{\beta\tau(U_p)}$, where $N_p=MN$; the constant $e^{-\beta N_p}$ cancels in normalized expectations. Apply [F6] to the positive face weights $w_p(U)=e^{\beta\tau(U)}$. In the tree gauge, the plaquette variables are independent and each has distribution $\nu_\beta$. [given, F1, F3, F6, algebra]
+
+1.2 Choose the tree gauge in [F6] with its vertical tree column equal to the left side $x=a$ of $C_{a,b;c,d}$. All horizontal links and the left-side vertical links are then the identity. For each row $j$, $P_{i,j}=V_{i+1,j}V_{i,j}^{-1}$ and $V_{a,j}=I_2$, so the recursion $V_{i+1,j}=P_{i,j}V_{i,j}$ yields $V_{b,j}=P_{b-1,j}\cdots P_{a,j}$. Traversing the rectangle from its lower-left corner, its bottom and top horizontal products are identities and its left vertical product is the identity, so $U_C$ is an ordered product of exactly the $(b-a)(d-c)=A$ plaquette matrices in the enclosed rectangle. [given, F1, F2, F6, step 1.1, algebra]
+
+1.3 Independence in [F6] lets us integrate the factors of this ordered product one at a time. By [F7], each matrix factor has expectation $\lambda I_2$, so the expected loop holonomy matrix is $(\lambda I_2)^A=\lambda^A I_2$. This entrywise iterated integration is valid because the finite group matrices are bounded and the product measure is a probability. [F6, F7, step 1.2, algebra]
+
+1.4 Taking half the trace gives $\langle W(C)\rangle_\beta=\lambda^A$. Since $0<\lambda<1$ by [F7], $\sigma_{\rm lat}=-\log\lambda$ is positive and $\lambda^A=e^{-\sigma_{\rm lat}A}$ for every positive integer area $A$. The conclusion is the stated finite-lattice model deduction only. [F2, F7, step 1.3, algebra] ∎
