items/lem-emg-fx-conformal-constraints.md:83:1.1 In any positively oriented coordinate chart, $\det h=\psi^{12}\det\bar h$, so $\sqrt{\det h}=\psi^6\sqrt{\det\bar h}$. The Levi-Civita formula and the determinant derivative give $\Gamma^i{}_{ik}=\partial_k\log\sqrt{\det h}$, hence $D_iV^i=(\sqrt{\det h})^{-1}\partial_i(\sqrt{\det h}\,V^i)$ for every smooth vector field $V$. Substituting $V=E=\psi^{-6}\bar E$ and then $V=B=\psi^{-6}\bar B$ gives $D_iE^i=\psi^{-6}\bar D_i\bar E^i$ and $D_iB^i=\psi^{-6}\bar D_i\bar B^i$. Since $e=\alpha^{-1}E$, $b=\alpha^{-1}B$, and both factors are positive, the two SI divergence constraints are equivalent to the two barred divergence equations. [given, F1, F2, algebra]
