items/post-fd-no-slip-newtonian.md:44:Let $I\subseteq\mathbb R$ be an open time interval in seconds and let $\Omega\subset\mathbb R^3$ be a fixed nonempty bounded open vessel in Cartesian coordinates measured in metres. Assume Countable Choice for the stated Sobolev space conventions. Define $D_\sigma(\Omega)=\{a\in C_c^\infty(\Omega;\mathbb R^3):\operatorname{div}a=0\}$, where divergence is the distributional divergence (equal to the classical divergence for these smooth fields), $H$ as its closure in $L^2(\Omega;\mathbb R^3)$, and $V$ as its closure in $H_0^1(\Omega;\mathbb R^3)$; here $H_0^1$ is the closure of compactly supported smooth vector fields in the $H^1$ norm, and $H^1$ uses square-integrable fields and first weak derivatives. The adopted no-slip condition means $u(t)\in V$, not a pointwise boundary value. This closure convention does not identify $V$ with every divergence-free member of $H_0^1$ on an arbitrary open set and does not assert a boundary trace theorem.
