items/def-emg-fx-stationary-axisymmetric-setup.md:53:Here $U(1)=\{z\in\mathbb C:|z|=1\}$ with complex multiplication and the smooth circle-group structure fixed in [[def-emg-local-potentials-and-circle-data]]. An **axial $U(1)$ action on $U$** is a specified smooth map $\rho:U(1)\times U\to U$ satisfying $\rho(1,p)=p$ and $\rho(z_1z_2,p)=\rho(z_1,\rho(z_2,p))$, with $\rho(z,\cdot)^*g=g$ for every $z$; effective means that only $z=1$ acts identically on all of $U$. Its generator is the smooth vector field $m$ defined by $m_p=\frac{d}{d\theta}|_{\theta=0}\rho(e^{i\theta},p)$; the parameter has period $2\pi$. Its **axis** is the fixed-point set $\mathcal A:=\{p\in U:\rho(z,p)=p\text{ for every }z\in U(1)\}$. For this page, an **axisymmetric region** is a region supplied with such an effective action and satisfying $g(m,m)>0$ on $U\setminus\mathcal A$. A stationary field and axial generator **commute** when their Lie bracket vanishes; in coordinates this means $\sum_a(k^a\partial_a m^b-m^a\partial_a k^b)=0$ for every component $b$.
