  | 
  | 5.1 In these variables the unnormalized density is exactly $\prod_{i,j}w_{i,j}(P_{i,j})$. Each positive continuous $w_{i,j}$ is bounded above and below by positive constants: continuity gives a bounded neighborhood at each group element, and compactness gives a finite subcover; applying the same argument to $1/w_{i,j}$ gives a positive lower bound. Thus each $z_{i,j}=\int_Gw_{i,j}\,d\mu$ is finite and strictly positive. The product Haar measure factors by step 4.1, so the partition function is $\prod_{i,j}z_{i,j}$; dividing by it yields the product of the displayed one-plaquette probabilities. [given, F1, F2, step 4.1, algebra] ∎
