  | 
  | [F4] [[lem-qftx-planar-plaquette-factorization]]: in a chosen tree gauge, the rectangle's plaquette holonomies are independent with law $\nu_\beta$ when all face weights are the same Wilson weight.
  | 
  | [F5] [[lem-qftx-su2-one-plaquette-average]]: $\mathbb E_{\nu_\beta}[U]=\lambda(\beta)I_2$ and $0<\lambda(\beta)<1$.
  | 
  | 
  | 
  | 1.1 The Wilson action weight is $e^{-\beta N_p}\prod_p e^{\beta\tau(U_p)}$, where $N_p=MN$; the constant $e^{-\beta N_p}$ cancels in normalized expectations. Since $\tau$ is real, conjugation invariant, and satisfies $\tau(U^{-1})=\tau(U)$, the positive continuous weights $w_p(U)=e^{\beta\tau(U)}$ satisfy [F4]'s hypotheses. Thus in the chosen tree gauge the plaquette variables are independent and each has law $\nu_\beta$. The inherited axiom base is $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$ [A1]. [given, A1, F1, F3, F4, algebra]
  | 
  | 2.1 Choose the tree gauge in [F4] with its vertical tree column equal to the left side $x=a$ of $C_{a,b;c,d}$. All horizontal links and the left-side vertical links are then the identity. For each row $j$, $P_{i,j}=V_{i+1,j}V_{i,j}^{-1}$ and $V_{a,j}=I_2$, so the recursion $V_{i+1,j}=P_{i,j}V_{i,j}$ yields $V_{b,j}=P_{b-1,j}\cdots P_{a,j}$. The counterclockwise boundary from $(a,c)$ therefore has ordered holonomy $U_C=(P_{b-1,d-1}\cdots P_{a,d-1})\cdots(P_{b-1,c}\cdots P_{a,c})$, a product of exactly $A=(b-a)(d-c)$ plaquette matrices. [given, F1, F2, F4, step 1.1, algebra]
  | 
  | 3.1 By [F4] the plaquette variables in this ordered product are independent; Fubini applied entry by entry to the finite product of bounded matrix entries replaces each factor by its expectation without changing the order. By [F5] each expectation is $\lambda I_2$, so the expected loop holonomy is $(\lambda I_2)^A=\lambda^A I_2$. [F4, F5, step 2.1, algebra]
  | 
