## Facts & Assumptions

**Given:** The finite link gauge action, a based closed edge word $C=(e_1,\ldots,e_\ell)$, and a finite-dimensional unitary representation $\rho$.

[F1] [[def-qftx-nonabelian-lattice-gauge-data]]: $(h\cdot U)_e=h_{s(e)}U_eh_{t(e)}^{-1}$ and a face or loop holonomy is the ordered product of its edge variables.

[F2] [[def-qftx-wilson-loop]]: $W_\rho(C;U)=d^{-1}\operatorname{Tr}(\rho(U_{e_1}\cdots U_{e_\ell}))$ for $d\geq1$.


## Proof

**Proof technique:** direct.

1.1 If $\ell=0$, both the loop holonomy and its conjugate are the identity. For $\ell\geq1$, write the successive vertices as $v_0,v_1,\ldots,v_\ell=v_0$. Substituting [F1] into the ordered product gives $U_C(h\cdot U)=(h_{v_0}U_{e_1}h_{v_1}^{-1})(h_{v_1}U_{e_2}h_{v_2}^{-1})\cdots(h_{v_{\ell-1}}U_{e_\ell}h_{v_0}^{-1})=h_{v_0}U_C(U)h_{v_0}^{-1}$, because each adjacent factor $h_{v_i}^{-1}h_{v_i}$ is the identity. [given, F1, algebra]

