+## Example
+
+For one square face with free boundary in the finite $SU(2)$ Wilson model at $0<\beta\leq1$, the normalized plaquette holonomy has law $d\nu_\beta(U)=z_\beta^{-1}e^{\beta\tau(U)}d\mu_2(U)$, where $\tau(U)=\tfrac12\operatorname{Tr}_2U$ and $z_\beta=\int e^{\beta\tau}d\mu_2$. The Wilson action partition factor is $Z_\square=e^{-\beta}z_\beta$, and the normalized fundamental Wilson loop around the square has expectation $\langle W(\partial\square)\rangle_\beta=\lambda(\beta)$, where $\lambda(\beta)=\int\tau e^{\beta\tau}d\mu_2/z_\beta=\beta/4+O(\beta^3)$ as $\beta\downarrow0$.
+
+## Example references
+
