        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $M,N\\geq1$ be integers and use the finite $M$-by-$N$ square lattice with free boundary (no periodic identifications and all boundary links retained), one $SU(2)$ link matrix per positively oriented edge, product normalized round measure, and only link variables (no matter variables), with the Wilson action $S_\\beta(U)=\\beta\\sum_p(1-\\tfrac12\\operatorname{Tr}_2 U_p)$. Use the defining two-dimensional representation and normalized Wilson loop $W(C)=\\tfrac12\\operatorname{Tr}_2 U_C$, with edge matrices multiplied in traversal order. Let $\\beta=4/g_0^2$ for dimensionless $g_0>0$, and restrict to the explicit strong-coupling window $0<\\beta\\leq1$ (equivalently $g_0^2\\geq4$). For any axis-aligned rectangle contained in the lattice with corners $(a,c)$ and $(b,d)$, where $0\\leq a<b\\leq M$ and $0\\leq c<d\\leq N$, let $C_{a,b;c,d}$ be its boundary traversed counterclockwise from $(a,c)$. Its area in plaquette units is $A=(b-a)(d-c)$. The defining representation has nontrivial $\\mathbb Z_2$ center charge because $-I_2$ acts as $-I_2$. Put\n\n$$\n\\lambda(\\beta):=\\frac{\\int_{SU(2)}\\tfrac12\\operatorname{Tr}_2(U)e^{\\beta\\operatorname{Tr}_2(U)/2}\\,d\\mu_2(U)}{\\int_{SU(2)}e^{\\beta\\operatorname{Tr}_2(U)/2}\\,d\\mu_2(U)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mu_2$ is normalized round measure on $SU(2)\\cong S^3$. Then $0<\\lambda(\\beta)<1$ and the exact finite-lattice expectation is\n\n$$\n\\langle W(C_{a,b;c,d})\\rangle_\\beta=\\lambda(\\beta)^A=\\exp\\!\\bigl(-\\sigma_{\\rm lat}(\\beta)A\\bigr),\\qquad \\sigma_{\\rm lat}(\\beta):=-\\log\\lambda(\\beta)>0.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $\\beta$ and the lattice string tension $\\sigma_{\\rm lat}$ are dimensionless. The identity holds for every finite container and every stated rectangle; no infinite-area, infinite-volume, or continuum limit is taken, and no continuum confinement or mass-gap claim follows.",
